# WAITS ON: feature-report.md A1 and A4 (the suffix bound; the implicit's two wordings).
#
# Eldritch gloves on a fractured base: essences, then the implicits.
#
# The base carries a fractured spell suppression roll, so every reforge keeps
# it. Deafening Essence of Greed guarantees life and is repeated until one
# elemental resistance lands at tier 1 (a Harvest swap can move it to the
# right element later). With the Eater dominant, an Eldritch Orb of Annulment
# only ever removes a suffix, which is how the guide opens a suffix slot
# without risking the life roll; losing the resistance sends the craft back to
# the essences. The implicits come last: embers until the Exarch one is right,
# then an Orb of Conflict raises the lower implicit and lowers the other, so
# the Eater side is refreshed with an ichor whenever it drops.

item {
    base:     "Dragonscale Gauntlets"
    ilvl:     86
    rarity:   rare
    suffixes: [ fractured "suppress spell damage" t2 ]
}

def anyEleRes(t) =
    has "fire resistance" t
    or has "cold resistance" t
    or has "lightning resistance" t

until anyEleRes(t1) {
    essence "greed" t1
}

# Make room on the suffix side under Eater dominance; the fractured mod and
# the prefixes are safe from an eldritch annul there.
if suffixCount == 3 {
    ichor lesser
    eldritch annul
    if not anyEleRes(t1) {
        restart
    }
}

bench "fire and chaos resistance"

# Implicits: embers until the Exarch implicit is the strike one, then raise it
# with Orbs of Conflict, topping the Eater side up whenever it is the lower.
until exarch "strike skills target 1" or exarch "strike skills target 2" {
    ember grand
}
until exarch exquisite "strike skills target 2" {
    conflict
    if dominant exarch {
        ichor exceptional
    }
}
